ion  our vision and make sure we're  respecting those elements and then the  strategic initiative  that we are implementing as an  organization all of that is critical and  if you if you allow your focus to wander  too much from those things it becomes  significant in the performance of the  business then ultimately all of those  things are very high-minded  but in addition to that the results of  the organization monitoring that  tweaking the business when it needs to  be tweaked looking at opportunities for  growth organic as well as acquisition so  that's where I spend most of my time  we're seeing some of the great interior  design work you do there and you're in  you know all those places around the  country yeah yeah that is actually a  passion of mine we started a group  actually just rebranded the group last  year it's called color art sports now  and like it has a Busch Stadium their  Busch Stadium yeah very good very good  we the reason why we got into color arts  sports was when Busch Stadium was being  renovated actually being rebuilt and  there was an opportunity there and  through a number of conversations with  the contractor Hunt's construction we  were able to open up a couple new doors  for us in that segment and as anyone  that's really engaged in the sports  scene these days realizes universities  colleges professional franchises are  renovating and building new stadiums at  a rapid pace and as you looked at that  you could see that we've done about 15  or 16 stadiums currently we'll really  yeah thank you thank you and we've  touched a large part of the nation for  opportunities where new stadiums are  coming on the ground that was Busch  Stadium you just saw up there and I  think we're also looking at Busch there  as well so this gives you a sampling  those images give you a nice sampling of  some of the projects we've done  nationally looking at all these other  place city I'm a New Yorker you're in  Citi Field with the New York Mets play  the myths yeah we did the myths it was  great mostly the Yankees up there though  by the way do you have a Yankee fan  there's a story would you like to hear  it please  we actually after we completed the Mets  the Yanks were due in their Stadium  shortly thereafter and  yeah exactly and we approach the Yanks  and and interesting learning moment  frankly we we said we did the Mets and  and you wouldn't have thought there was  intermurals between the Mets and the  eggs  yeah well that's it that was a done deal  exactly right it was a national league  an American League team and I was not on  that but it was sorry yeah  tell us you there's something  interesting over in your bio that I  think really pertains to chess and our  chess fans out there the the you read a  book called in search of excellence  that's actually prompted you to be  become a part of this company which  you've been at now since 85 what's a  secret proposition to the success in  your company and and how does that  connect back to chest as you can see it  the idea that you know what what is it  about excellence and striving for it  that keeps a company like yours that  what gives a winning edge and you know  if you don't want to tell too many trade  secrets because you've got competitors  out there we'll keep it a secret yeah  okay we will do that we was not really  being broadcast to all over the world I  understand it block out the if you take  a look at our mission and vision and  those are our core beliefs if you go out  on our website color - art comm you'll  you'll see what our secret sauce is we  don't we don't really keep it undercover  at all we really focus on connecting  using knowledge to connect people in  space and believe it or not these days  c-suite executives are really spending a  lot of time focusing on collaboration in  their corporate environment attracting  retaining and engaging and that is the  most part most important part and there  there is a belief today that has shaped  up that space for a long time was viewed  as an expense in other words  it's something that hits the PNL and  costs us money today space is viewed as  an asset in categories of optimizing  real estate and so forth  so what do we do to facilitate that we  try and bring knowledge to the table in  every engagement that we have with a  client that comes in a lot of forms  primary research case studies insights  secondary research reaching out to some  of the academics around the world the  Harvard Business Review I actually had a  client the other day in a major st.  Louis company say to me Gary I really am  NOT interested in what's going on in  space today but can you tell me what's  going to be happening in the next two to  three years and that moment was an  eye-opening moment for me that we we are  on the right path in terms of using  research to advance companies in the st.  Louis and the region final question for  you you're a chess player I am how does  chess help you in your day-to-day role I  think the easy answer on that is it  helps you with strategy and so forth and  that's true it does but it builds  character  it really does build character and I'm  not stealing that from you I researched  you a little bit as well and I saw that  you you talked about character in one of  your books and character in individuals  is essential I I find that the ability  to implement to be able to stay the  course on a chess game stay focused on a  chess game drives parts of your brain  that frankly you don't even know is  being impacted I watch basketball a lot  the n-c-double-a s are going on right  now and I've started to look at  basketball believe it or not from a  strategic viewpoint that I never did  before until I started getting reengaged  in chess I can see why you're the boss  man for all these years thank you they  keep you around thank you very much for  your generous support in color art take  a look at their website folks great work  and great support for all that is chess  here in st. Louis question for you are  you a daddy are you a father right I am  a father yeah and do you teach your  children chess do you engage oh my  daughter happens to be standing right  over there right  that's Kelly hey Kelly  are you a chess player honest answer we  have good news for you we have ladies  night chess classes here on Thursday  nights wine cheese and chess lessons you  can't go wrong thank you Gary and thank  you for your support it's very very nice  thanks so much

